MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When exporting lots of trees into a pdf file, one tree a page, how to adjust the height of different page.
Because of different number of taxa in trees, the figure generated by either the specified height or the default value of "pdf()" function in R
looks very bad. Any suggestion would be appreciated.

My code:

pdf("group_tree.pdf", onefile = T, width= 10, height = 14)
# pdf("test-page-height.pdf", onefile= T)

for (i in seq.int(TREE))
{

  title <- sub(".*(arCOG\\d+)$", "\\1", TREE[i], perl=T)
  tree <- read.tree(TREE[i])
  tree <- fortify(tree)
 p<-ggtree(tree.df) %<+% LS +
    geom_text2(aes(label = label,subset = !isTip),nudge_x = -0.015,nudge_y = 0.5,size = 2.5)+
    geom_tiplab(size=2, aes(label= label2)) +
    geom_point(size= 2.5, aes(color= group, shape= group))+
    scale_color_manual(values= colorset) +
    scale_shape_manual(values= shapeset)+
    ggtitle(title)
  print (p)
}
dev.off()

